WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.344
After Xia lost power, the royal house was greatly weakened.

00:00:04.694 --> 00:00:08.414
Shao Kang slowly grew up in difficult circumstances.

00:00:08.764 --> 00:00:13.540
Hardworking and enduring, he learned how to govern a place well.

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:18.354
Many people sympathized with the Xia royal house and were willing to help Shao Kang.

00:00:18.704 --> 00:00:23.576
Gradually Shao Kang gained supporters, and his strength slowly grew.

00:00:23.926 --> 00:00:27.742
He rallied the royal house's old followers and the common people.

00:00:28.092 --> 00:00:32.172
Shao Kang led everyone to recover the lost lands.

00:00:32.522 --> 00:00:36.242
After great effort, they finally defeated Han Zhuo's forces.

00:00:36.592 --> 00:00:41.752
Shao Kang restored the rule of Xia, and the people cheered in celebration.

00:00:42.102 --> 00:00:46.350
Order returned to the capital, and people lived in peace and contentment.

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:51.212
Later generations called this story the Revival under Shao Kang.

00:00:51.562 --> 00:00:55.858
A revival means regaining strength after a time of decline.

